    "body": "## Motivation\n\nSince #32272, `MHATokenToKVPool` stores each layer's K and V as two halves of one allocation. On ROCm this breaks Mooncake PD transfers: decode receives corrupted KV without any transfer error. In `stage-b-test-large-8-gpu-mi35x-disaggregation-amd`, `test_disaggregation_basic.py` (Qwen3-8B, Mooncake) dropped from 0.955 GSM8K accuracy to 0.0-0.01 on main ([example job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40503413710/job/122186653097)). NIXL and MORI tests in the same job are unaffected (NIXL GSM8K 0.765 before and after).\n\nThe last passing main run was at 5884e4fec; the failures start with the commit range that includes #32272. The other candidates in that range don't touch this path for a bf16 Qwen3 PD run.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSkip the fused K/V allocation on ROCm (`and not _is_hip`) and keep separate per-layer K and V buffers, as before #32272. The fused layout serves the CUDA trtllm fmha_v2 paged kernels, which don't run on ROCm. Other platforms are unchanged.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `stage-b-test-large-8-gpu-mi35x-disaggregation-amd` on rocm10, dispatched on this commit: all four files pass. `test_disaggregation_basic.py` GSM8K 0.950 / 0.965, `test_disaggregation_pp.py` 0.945-0.955, NIXL 0.770, MORI OK ([job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40549450596/job/122349178411)).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40555506148](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40555506148)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40555506102](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40555506102)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40555506196](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40555506196)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
